# Catalog writes only

Studio agents may `write_file` **only** paths listed for that agent in
`skills/workspace-handoff`. Git stays in GitHub (`github_get_file`). Do not
dump git (catalog, matrix, configs) into the workspace so a script can run.

When authoring a prompt or skill:

- Name the catalog files, plus schema + example to fill.
- Inline the fleet FS contract: built-in `read_file`/`write_file` are
  workspace-relative; never `/shared_workspace/` (UUID workspace
  paths included), `sessions/`, or `Internal directory`. MiniMax
  Lifecycle sandbox: Access denied listing `file_explorer` → retry
  `file_explorer/<catalog row>` once. Do not author a blanket “never
  `file_explorer`” on that agent — that is why it retries UUID paths.
- Hard no: helper `.py`, `_git_input.json`, `prepare_*`, `health-board.md`,
  or any path not in the catalog.
- Health Analyzer is the template: one (or few) named writes.

Do not add a scratch workspace file to make a Python join easier. Put
inputs in git or MCP results; put outputs in the catalog row.
